# HELP llmgateway_requests_total Total requests admitted for accounting today (UTC calendar day; resets at UTC midnight), by scope. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_requests_total counter
llmgateway_requests_total{scope_kind="user",scope_id="alice"} 0
llmgateway_requests_total{scope_kind="group",scope_id="default"} 0
llmgateway_requests_total{scope_kind="total",scope_id="all"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_tokens_total Total tokens accounted today (UTC calendar day; resets at UTC midnight), by scope and direction. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_tokens_total counter
llmgateway_tokens_total{scope_kind="user",scope_id="alice",direction="prompt"} 0
llmgateway_tokens_total{scope_kind="user",scope_id="alice",direction="completion"} 0
llmgateway_tokens_total{scope_kind="group",scope_id="default",direction="prompt"} 0
llmgateway_tokens_total{scope_kind="group",scope_id="default",direction="completion"} 0
llmgateway_tokens_total{scope_kind="total",scope_id="all",direction="prompt"} 0
llmgateway_tokens_total{scope_kind="total",scope_id="all",direction="completion"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_cost_micro_usd_total Total cost accounted today (UTC calendar day; resets at UTC midnight), in micro-USD (1000000 = $1), by scope. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_cost_micro_usd_total counter
llmgateway_cost_micro_usd_total{scope_kind="user",scope_id="alice"} 0
llmgateway_cost_micro_usd_total{scope_kind="group",scope_id="default"} 0
llmgateway_cost_micro_usd_total{scope_kind="total",scope_id="all"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_budget_consumed_ratio Fraction of a configured limit already consumed in its own window; 1.0 means fully consumed, above 1.0 means the limit has been breached. Emitted only for a scope with that particular limit configured. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_budget_consumed_ratio gauge
# HELP llmgateway_provider_attempts_total Total upstream attempts today (UTC calendar day; resets at UTC midnight), by provider. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_provider_attempts_total counter
llmgateway_provider_attempts_total{provider="alpha"} 0
llmgateway_provider_attempts_total{provider="beta"} 0
llmgateway_provider_attempts_total{provider="gamma"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_provider_failures_total Total upstream attempts today classified as a provider fault (transport error, 429, or 5xx — the same classification recordProviderAttempt/isTransient apply), by provider. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_provider_failures_total counter
llmgateway_provider_failures_total{provider="alpha"} 0
llmgateway_provider_failures_total{provider="beta"} 0
llmgateway_provider_failures_total{provider="gamma"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_provider_healthy 1 when the provider's discovery circuit breaker is not open (closed or half-open), 0 when open (discoveryHealthy, registry.go). AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with redis.sharedState on, the discovery circuit breaker is shared via Redis, so every replica reports the same value and max() is correct. Without it, each replica runs its own breaker, so the value can differ per replica; use min() to surface "at least one replica sees this provider as unhealthy". sum() is meaningless for a 0/1 gauge.
# TYPE llmgateway_provider_healthy gauge
llmgateway_provider_healthy{provider="alpha"} 1
llmgateway_provider_healthy{provider="beta"} 1
llmgateway_provider_healthy{provider="gamma"} 1
# HELP llmgateway_provider_model_attempts_total Total upstream attempts today (UTC calendar day; resets at UTC midnight), by provider and model. Opt-in via metrics.modelLabel — see MetricsConfig's own doc comment for the cardinality trade-off. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_provider_model_attempts_total counter
llmgateway_provider_model_attempts_total{provider="alpha",model="a1"} 0
llmgateway_provider_model_attempts_total{provider="alpha",model="a2"} 0
llmgateway_provider_model_attempts_total{provider="beta",model="b1"} 0
llmgateway_provider_model_attempts_total{provider="gamma",model="c1"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_provider_model_failures_total Total upstream attempts today classified as a provider fault, by provider and model. Opt-in via metrics.modelLabel. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: with Redis configured, this value is the gateway-wide total read from shared limit state and is IDENTICAL on every replica's own /metrics response — aggregate with max(), never sum(), or a multi-replica deployment overcounts by the replica count. Without Redis (the in-memory fallback), this SAME family becomes genuinely per-process instead, and sum() becomes the correct aggregation. Know which one you are running.
# TYPE llmgateway_provider_model_failures_total counter
llmgateway_provider_model_failures_total{provider="alpha",model="a1"} 0
llmgateway_provider_model_failures_total{provider="alpha",model="a2"} 0
llmgateway_provider_model_failures_total{provider="beta",model="b1"} 0
llmgateway_provider_model_failures_total{provider="gamma",model="c1"} 0
# HELP llmgateway_upstream_ttfb_seconds Time to first successful byte read from an upstream response body, in seconds, measured from just before the request was sent (watchdogBody, timeout.go). Meaningful as a distinct "how fast did the provider start responding" signal only for stream="true": a non-streaming provider buffers its whole completion before sending anything, so its own TTFB is approximately equal to its own llmgateway_upstream_duration_seconds and carries the same output-length contamination duration does — always split by the stream label before comparing across requests of different lengths, never averaged across it. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: this histogram lives only in this process's memory, never in Redis, regardless of Config.Redis — each replica reports only the upstream traffic it personally handled, so aggregate with sum() (histogram_quantile over a sum()-aggregated set, for a real percentile), which is always correct for it, unlike the store-backed families above that flip between sum() and max() depending on whether Redis is configured.
# TYPE llmgateway_upstream_ttfb_seconds histogram
llmgateway_upstream_ttfb_seconds_bucket{provider="alpha",stream="false",le="0.1"} 1
llmgateway_upstream_ttfb_seconds_bucket{provider="alpha",stream="false",le="0.25"} 1
