# HELP llmgateway_rate_limit_rejections_total Total requests refused by a rate or budget limit since process start, by scope. Unlike the request/token/cost counters above, this is a process-lifetime counter, not UTC-day-windowed, but it does NOT reset only on restart: a scope's own count resets to 0 when that user is removed via a hot-reloaded users file, and every tracked scope resets together, in one bulk cliff (not a graceful per-scope decay), the instant more than 2000 distinct scopes have ever been seen — a value that drops is one of these events, not a scrape anomaly. AGGREGATION ACROSS REPLICAS: this counter lives only in this process's memory, never in Redis, regardless of Config.Redis — aggregate with sum(), which is always correct for it, unlike the store-backed families above.
# TYPE llmgateway_rate_limit_rejections_total counter
llmgateway_rate_limit_rejections_total{scope_kind="user",scope_id="alice"} 2
